{section: 1}
[Gm]Da bi naši starci znali || If only our old folks knew
[Cm]kakvo je [Gm]življenje, || what kind of life this is,
[Gm]kud si deca kruha služe, || where their children earn their bread:
samo [Bb]je [D]kamenje. || there is nothing but stone.

{section: 2}
[Bb]Oj ti Filak, [Cm]glavni varoš, || Oh you, Filak, the main town,
[Gm]kak si [F]v [Gm]hudom mesti, || what a harsh place you stand in,
[~Gm]gora i sam živi kamen, || mountains and nothing but bare rock,
nega [~Bb]kaj za [~D]jesti. || there is nothing to eat.

{section: 3}
[Gm]Da bi vnoga majka znala, || If many a mother knew,
[Cm]bi se ras[Gm]plakala, || she would burst into tears,
[Gm]kud si sinek kruha služi, || where her little son earns his bread,
de ga [Bb]ne[D]ga polja. || where there are no fields.

{section: 4}
[Bb]Bole daj me [Cm]ne bi bila || It would have been better
[Gm]majči[F]ca ro[Gm]dila, || if my dear mother had never borne me,
[~Gm]neg kaj me je ovak dalko || than to let me go so far away
po [~Bb]sveto pu[~D]stila. || out into the world.
